=== layout: multiple-choice

@question

*Your Turn: Recognizing Homologs*

Two chromosome 14 [*homologs*]{color=#24578F}: what should they have in common? *Select all that apply.*

- A. Similar length
- B. Same centromere position
- C. Same banding pattern
- D. The same genes at corresponding locations
- E. Always an X shape, even before DNA replication

@answer

A, B, C, and D.

=== layout: one-panel

# Recognizing Homologs: Explanation

@body

- [*A, B, C, and D*]{color=#007A00}
- [*Homologs*]{color=#24578F}: same genes; possibly different alleles
- [*X shape*]{color=#935D00}: after DNA replication
- Replicated homolog: *two sister chromatids*
- Before replication: *the same chromosome*

=== layout: subsection

# Chromosome Painting

=== layout: one-panel

# Chromosome Painting

@body

- [*DNA probes*]{color=#24578F}: binding to matching chromosome sequences
- [*FISH*]{color=#935D00}: fluorescence in situ hybridization
- Fluorescent labels: visible chromosome sequences
- [*Chromosome painting*]{color=#24578F}: probe mixtures; different chromosome colors

=== layout: one-panel

