# Human Chromosome 2: A Fusion

@body

![Lecture diagram](assets/visual_renewal/human_chromosome_2_fusion.drawn.svg)

- Two functional centromeres can make a chromosome unstable.
- The centromere in the long arm became inactivated.
- DNA remnants of the ancestral centromere are still detectable.

@citation

https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/1587535/

@notes

Two ancestral chromosomes joined. One centromere became inactive. Two active centromeres can make a chromosome unstable.

